---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Open Source" description="The tools we build and release — killdate-kit, Orrery, vizstack, and agentviz. Free, local-first, no accounts.">

  <div class="intro">
    <p class="section-label">Langmerge Agentic Systems Lab — Open Source</p>
    <h1>Open Source</h1>
    <p class="tagline">The tools we build for our own work and release for yours. Free, local-first, no accounts.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tool-list">

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="tool-meta">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/killdate-kit" class="tool-title" target="_blank" rel="noopener">killdate-kit</a>
        <span class="tool-tag">starter repo</span>
      </div>
      <p class="tool-desc">The repo we fork every time we start something new — a pre-wired CLAUDE.md, Cursor rules, and a runbook system, so the AI tools have structure to push against. The playbook walks through how we actually use it.</p>
      <div class="tool-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/killdate-kit" class="tool-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
        <a href="/playbook" class="tool-link">The playbook →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="tool-meta">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/orrery" class="tool-title" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Orrery</a>
        <span class="tool-tag">desktop app</span>
      </div>
      <p class="tool-desc">One local window for every project's live git state and the facts you normally keep in your head — plus what your agents left behind across repos, sessions, and worktrees. Reads your disk live: no server, no account, no telemetry. Formerly Mission Control.</p>
      <div class="tool-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/orrery" class="tool-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
        <a href="/posts/mission-control" class="tool-link">How it was built →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="tool-meta">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/vizstack" class="tool-title" target="_blank" rel="noopener">vizstack</a>
        <span class="tool-tag">cli</span>
      </div>
      <p class="tool-desc">A zero-install CLI that turns any Remix or Next.js codebase into an interactive dependency map. Point it at a directory and it produces a single HTML file showing your routes, database, AI providers, and external APIs as a scrollable graph — hover any node to see what connects to it.</p>
      <a href="/tools/ecosystem-viz.html" class="viz-preview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img src="/images/ecosystem-viz-preview.png" alt="Shelf ecosystem cross-layer dependency map — routes, database, AI layer, external APIs" class="viz-img" />
        <span class="viz-caption">Open interactive map →</span>
      </a>
      <div class="tool-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/vizstack" class="tool-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
        <a href="/posts/18-remix-route-visualizer" class="tool-link">How it was built →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="tool-meta">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/agentviz" class="tool-title" target="_blank" rel="noopener">agentviz</a>
        <span class="tool-tag">cli</span>
      </div>
      <p class="tool-desc">vizstack's sibling for Python agent pipelines, where routes are the wrong shape. Point it at a pipeline and get one interactive HTML file: which stages call which models, where they touch the database, what's cached versus recomputed, what's traced versus flying blind.</p>
      <div class="tool-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/agentviz" class="tool-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .intro h1 {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .tagline {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #888;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .tool-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }

  .tool {
    padding: 32px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .tool:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }

  .tool-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .tool-title {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  .tool-title:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .tool-tag {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    background: var(--border);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .tool-desc {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .tool-links { display: flex; gap: 20px; }

  .tool-link {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: opacity 0.15s;
  }

  .tool-link:hover { opacity: 0.7; }

  .viz-preview {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .viz-preview:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }

  .viz-img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

  .viz-caption {
    display: block;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: #0f0f0f;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .tool-meta { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
    .tool-title { font-size: 15px; }
    .tool { padding: 24px 0; }
    .viz-caption { font-size: 11px; }
  }
</style>
